    "_comment": "Narrower follow-up to agv_congestion_sweep.json. That run found a deadlock cliff: at agvCount=8, only LPT_MMUR/LRT_MMUR survive (7/9 rules gridlock); by agvCount=12, ALL rules gridlock (permanent circular-wait in TrafficZone.TryReserve -- see segment_congestion block_events in the millions with near-zero traversals). This sweep pins the two thresholds precisely: 6/7 (where the non-MMUR majority starts failing, between the healthy agvCount=5 and the agvCount=8 collapse) and 9/10/11 (where MMUR itself gives out, between the agvCount=8 survivors and the agvCount=12 total collapse). Run with MAX_EPISODE_SIM_SECONDS lowered to 100000 so a deadlocked config fails in ~10-15 min instead of ~4 hours.",
